      "problem": "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $9?$\n\nI. $7\\,050\\,113$\n\nII. $5\\,119\\,232$\n\nIII. $14\\,624\\,100$",
      "worked_solution": "A number is divisible by $9$ if the sum of its digits is divisible by $9.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $7\\,050\\,113$ is\n\n$$\n7+0+5+0+1+1+3=17,\n$$\n\nwhich is *not* divisible by $9.$ So, $7\\,050\\,113$ is *not* divisible by $9.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $5\\,119\\,232$ is\n\n$$\n5+1+1+9+2+3+2=23,\n$$\n\nwhich is *not* divisible by $9.$ So, $5\\,119\\,232$ is *not* divisible by $9.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $14\\,624\\,100$ is\n\n$$\n1+4+6+2+4+1+0+0=18,\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $9.$ So, $14\\,624\\,100$ is divisible by $9.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"llI only.\"",
